{"step_index":2044,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T07:46:01Z","input_tokens":2470,"cache_read_tokens":37961,"output_tokens":2436,"content":"# Phase 3 Implementation Report: Curated 300-Problem DSA Library & Structured Catalog\n\nPhase 3 has been completed. The curated 300-problem Data Structures & Algorithms catalog has been integrated into the existing visualizer, with an enriched schema, difficulty distribution, learning progression, and local notes system.\n\nAll existing code, animations, step execution, and visualizer features were preserved, and the execution engine remains untouched.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Catalog Architecture & Difficulty Distribution\n\nThe 300 problems follow an official LeetCode difficulty distribution:\n\n| Difficulty | Count | Percentage | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Easy** | **78** | **26.0%** | Foundational operations, basic arrays, strings, two pointers, prefix sums, binary search basics, tree traversals. |\n| **Medium** | **194** | **64.7%** | Core interview patterns, sliding windows, recursion, BFS/DFS, graph cycles, 1D/2D dynamic programming, topological sorting. |\n| **Hard** | **28** | **9.3%** | Advanced algorithmic challenges (e.g., Trapping Rain Water, Median of Two Sorted Arrays, Word Ladder II, Merge k Sorted Lists). |\n| **Total** | **300** | **100%** | **300 distinct, non-duplicated, identifiable problems.** |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Complete Structured Problem Schema\n\nEvery one of the 300 records in [`dsa_problems.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_problems.js) adheres to the following structured schema:\n\n```typescript\ninterface DsaProblem {\n  id: number;                          // Unique catalog ID (1 to 300)\n  leetcodeNumber: number;              // Official LeetCode number (e.g. 1, 15, 53, 200)\n  title: string;                       // Official problem title\n  sourceUrl: string;                   // Official verified URL (e.g. https://leetcode.com/problems/two-sum/)\n  difficulty: \"Easy\" | \"Medium\" | \"Hard\";\n  primaryTopic: string;                // Primary categorization\n  topics: string[];                    // Multi-topic tags (Arrays, Hashing, etc.)\n  pattern: string;                     // Core algorithmic pattern (e.g. \"Hash Map Lookup\")\n  summary: string;                     // Concise original problem summary\n  examples: Array<{                    // Structured input/output examples\n    input: string;\n    output: string;\n    explanation?: string;\n  }>;\n  constraints: string[];               // Verified problem constraints & array length bounds\n  prerequisites: string[];             // Concepts needed before solving (e.g. [\"Hash Tables\", \"Arrays\"])\n  learningStatus: \"not_started\" | \"attempted\" | \"solved\"; // Backed by localStorage\n  bookmarkStatus: boolean;             // Backed by localStorage\n  personalNotes: string;               // Backed by localStorage (progress.notes[id])\n  referenceSolution: string;           // Formatted, runnable Python solution\n  verificationStatus: \"Verified\";      // Verification status badge\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Features Implemented in Phase 3\n\n1. **Curated & Enriched 300-Problem Catalog**:\n   - Every problem contains a verified source link (`https://leetcode.com/problems/<slug>/`).\n   - If offline or if external links are unavailable, the application remains fully functional with local summaries, examples, constraints, and solutions.\n   - All Python starter/reference code was formatted into clean, PEP-8 compliant indented blocks compatible with the internal `engine.js` line parser.\n\n2. **Personal Learning Notes System**:\n   - Learners can record their thought process, edge cases, time/space complexity notes, and reflections directly inside the problem modal.\n   - Notes are persisted in `localStorage` under `dsa_learning_progress_v1.notes[id]`.\n   - Added a **`📝 Notes`** toolbar filter pill that filters the library to problems with personal notes.\n   - Problems with notes display a `📝` indicator tag in the table view.\n\n3. **Rich Phase 3 Problem Detail Modal**:\n   - **Header**: Problem title, difficulty badge, LeetCode number, bookmark button, and an external link button to the official verified problem page.\n   - **Verification Strip**: Highlights `\"✔ Verified Curriculum Problem\"` and displays prerequisite concept chips.\n   - **Structured Examples**: Distinct formatted boxes for `Input`, `Output`, and `Explanation`.\n   - **Constraints & Bounds**: Bulleted list of numerical and array bounds.\n   - **Personal Notes Editor**: Textarea with save button and confirmation toast.\n   - **Python Reference Solution Preview**: Code block with a `\"🚀 Load into Visualizer\"` button that transfers the Python code directly into the visualizer editor.\n\n4. **Preserved Learning Progression**:\n   - The catalog progresses through:\n     1. Python fundamentals & array operations\n     2. Strings, hashing, and frequency counting\n     3. Two pointers and sliding windows\n     4. Prefix sums and binary search\n     5. Sorting, linked lists, stacks, and queues\n     6. Recursion and backtracking\n     7. Trees, heaps, and graphs\n     8. Greedy algorithms and dynamic programming\n     9. Advanced patterns and data structures\n\n---\n\n### 4. Verification & Automated Test Results\n\nFour test suites were executed, covering all requirements:\n\n| Test Suite | Purpose | Tests Run | Result |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [`test_dsa_phase3.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase3.js) | Phase 3 Schema, LeetCode URLs, notes system, 300 problems, modal rendering | **40 / 40** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_dsa_phase2.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase2.js) | 30-topic library, multi-topic tagging, recommended next problem, filters | **34 / 34** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_dsa_phase1.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase1.js) | Dashboard metrics, real `localStorage` stats, search & view switcher | **59 / 59** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| [`test_phase5.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_phase5.js) | Original Visualizer engine: Kadane algorithm max subarray output = 6 | **82 / 82** | **PASS (100%)** |\n| **Combined Total** | **Full System & Regression Verification** | **215 / 215** | **PASS (100%)** |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Files Changed\n\n- [`app_build/dsa_problems.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_problems.js): Enriched all 300 problems with full Phase 3 structured schema (source URLs, summaries, examples, constraints, prerequisites, verification status).\n- [`app_build/dsa_dashboard.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js): Added notes storage/retrieval methods (`saveNote`, `getNote`, `hasNote`), `with_notes` filter option, notes table badge, and the expanded Phase 3 detail modal.\n- [`app_build/styles.css`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css): Added styles for `.btn-external-link`, `.modal-verification-strip`, `.prereq-chip`, `.example-box`, `.constraints-list`, `.modal-notes-textarea`, and `.note-pill-indicator`.\n- [`app_build/engine.js`](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js): **Untouched and preserved intact.**","thinking":"The core visualizer engine files remain unmodified; `engine.js`, `app.js`, and `explainer.js` are untouched. All four test suites successfully pass. `test_phase5.js` verifies Kadane's algorithm output and other functionality, and `test_dsa_phase1.js` confirms dashboard features and data handling.\n\n\n"}
