n75:       name: 'Stacks',\r\n76:       icon: '🥞',\r\n77:       category: 'Data Structures',\r\n78:       color: '#8b5cf6',\r\n79:       summary: 'Last-In-First-Out (LIFO) structure. Invaluable for nested bracket validation, function call simulation, undo mechanisms, and expression evaluation.'\r\n80:     },\r\n81:     {\r\n82:       name: 'Queues and Deques',\r\n83:       icon: '🚶‍♂️',\r\n84:       category: 'Data Structures',\r\n85:       color: '#7c3aed',\r\n86:       summary: 'First-In-First-Out (FIFO) and double-ended queues. Fundamental for breadth-first search (BFS) level-order traversal and sliding window extrema.'\r\n87:     },\r\n88:     {\r\n89:       name: 'Recursion',\r\n90:       icon: '🔄',\r\n91:       category: 'Techniques & Patterns',\r\n92:       color: '#ec4899',\r\n93:       summary: 'Self-referential function execution solving smaller instances of the same problem. Master base cases, recursion stack frames, and recursive tree branches.'\r\n94:     },\r\n95:     {\r\n96:       name: 'Backtracking',\r\n97:       icon: '↩️',\r\n98:       category: 'Techniques & Patterns',\r\n99:       color: '#f97316',\r\n100:       summary: 'Systematic depth-first exploration of state-space decision trees that prunes invalid candidates and backtracks state to generate combinations and permutations.'\r\n101:     },\r\n102:     {\r\n103:       name: 'Trees and Binary Trees',\r\n104:       icon: '🌳',\r\n105:       category: 'Data Structures',\r\n106:       color: '#15803d',\r\n107:       summary: 'Hierarchical node graphs with a single root and at most two children per node. Master preorder, inorder, postorder DFS, and level-order BFS.'\r\n108:     },\r\n109:     {\r\n110:       name: 'Binary Search Trees',\r\n111:       icon: '🌲',\r\n112:       category: 'Data Structures',\r\n113:       color: '#166534',\r\n114:       summary: 'Binary trees where left subtree keys are smaller and right subtree keys are larger. Guarantees sorted in-order traversal and O(h) search and